 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by Dublin,\nThe ruddy sunbreaks the wondrous fire;\nI have seen it softly gone below them,\nAnd left him, to let his memory live.\nHe never was: \"Nothing's more divine\nThan the rest when they are all apart.\"[793a. A\nThere's no doubt that you'll find me fond again,\nWhen evening is over and I'm away;\nI've met with another friend again,\nAnd shall go at once to meet again.\nWhy did I not look into my memories,\nTo see if any note should answer then?",
